+// "Always" rule: "The client signs the anchor challenge in their own
+// wallet; Pactly never holds a key"). These two functions split the same
+// exchange into a request half (this backend only fetches and validates the
+// challenge) and a submit half (this backend only relays what the client's
+// own wallet already signed), so a route can hand the unsigned challenge to
+// the frontend and receive the signed one back, with no signer ever passing
+// through this backend. Deliberately not implemented by refactoring
+// `runAnchorSep10` into shared internals: that function is this session's
